// Verilator arguments for the core-level simulation of the CRAY X-MP core
// (module emu of Cray-XMP.sv).  The HDL file list comes from files.qip (see
// tools/py/qip2vc.py); the framework's modules are stand-ins (sim/stubs).  A
// millisecond is 105,263 clocks of the CPU, as in
// the core.  Of the memories only the first 4,096 words are zeroed at the
// start, not all eight million: the model of DDR3 holds zeros anyway.
// Warnings of style are for `make lint`; they are switched off here as a group,
// because the names of single ones differ from one Verilator to the next.
--cc --exe --build -j 0
--top-module emu
-GCLEAR=25'd4096
-Wno-fatal -Wno-lint -Wno-style -Wno-WIDTH -Wno-UNUSED -Wno-PINMISSING -Wno-DECLFILENAME -Wno-TIMESCALEMOD
-Wno-CASEINCOMPLETE -Wno-CASEX -Wno-BLKSEQ -Wno-UNDRIVEN -Wno-EOFNEWLINE -Wno-PINCONNECTEMPTY
-O3 --x-assign fast --x-initial fast
-CFLAGS "-O2 -std=c++17"
-I. -Isim/stubs -Irtl/terminal -Irtl/cray/cray-1x
sim/stubs/hps_io.sv
sim/stubs/pll.v
sim/stubs/video.sv
-f sim/build/core.files
sim/harness/core_main.cpp
